      {
        "id": 60347,
        "name": "Pydro",
        "username": "Pydro",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/pydro/{size}/1844_2.png",
        "created_at": "2013-04-18T17:04:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>*cracks knuckles*</p><p>Ok give me a min to write this up.</p><p>When removing tokens (either from taking damage in battle or through various card effects) you follow the following&nbsp;3 rules:</p><p>1) Remove ALL defense tokens before removing any weapon tokens.</p><p>2) Tokens must be removed from techs before taking them from the ship itself (your in a fierce dogfight and they shoot out your brand new [redacted])</p><p>3) Remove tokens from the newest tech first.</p><p>Using these 3 rules we can come up with a definitive list of how to remove token:</p><p>1) Remove defensive token them from the newest defensive tech (if there is more damage proceed to the next newewst, etc).</p><p>2) Remove defensive tokens from the ship.</p><p>3) Remove&nbsp;weapon token them from the newest&nbsp;weapon tech (if there is more damage proceed to the next newewst, etc).</p><p>4) Removie weapon tokens from the ship.</p><p>&nbsp;</p><p>Knowing these rules are very importantn for 2 reasons:</p><p>1) It allows you to protect and cover a tech that you want by installing another tech over it.</p><p>2) Many techs and effects upon destruction. Planning ahead so that you know what will be destroyed if I do X can have some fantastic effects.</p>",
